facing"],"finding":"The plan states the lock-TTL override environment variable is `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS`, but the upstream awslabs/git-remote-s3 README names it `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL` (no `_SECONDS` suffix). This unverified capability assertion will be copied verbatim into operator-facing docs (`docs/s3-backend.md`) and the ADR, so an incorrect env-var name would silently fail to override the TTL for operators.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa17b9dd50ad5f27d","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2(e) and step 3; AC line 2 (docs/s3-backend.md self-heal subsection)","norm_id":"ncd8446b7b3168d88","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["An operator copies `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` from the docs, sets it, and the TTL is not actually overridden because the real variable is `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL`."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Change `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` to `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL` (confirming against the `git-remote-s3>=0.3.2` release you pin), and likewise confirm the internal constant name (`DEFAULT_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS`) before citing it.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Before publishing, verify git-remote-s3's `DEFAULT_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` name, its 60s value, and the `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` override env-var name against the installed helper's source/--help at the pinned >=0.3.2 (record MATCH/MISMATCH), or soften the doc to describe a bounded auto-steal delay without asserting the exact identifiers/value.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: \"git-remote-s3's `DEFAULT_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` = 60s, overridable via the `GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS` env var\"","search_files for DEFAULT_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS, GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS, and TTL under src/rebar/_store all return (no matches) — the names are absent from the repo","resolve_symbol git_remote_s3 => UNRESOLVED (cannot probe the constant/env-var against upstream source)","src/rebar/_store/push.py:341 uses rebar's own `_lock.LockTimeout`, a distinct lock from git-remote-s3's S3 object lock the TTL governs","EVIDENCE CLASS: Partially-verified — integration exists and is used, but this specific lock-TTL surface (constant name, env-var name, 60s value) is unconfirmed"],"finding":"The plan publishes git-remote-s3's stale-lock TTL surface to operators (DEFAULT_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS = 60s, override env var GIT_REMOTE_S3_LOCK_TTL_SECONDS) as authoritative documentation, but these specific identifier names and the 60-second value are unverified against upstream --help/source: neither string appears anywhere in the rebar repo, the library is not importable in this environment, and rebar's own lock code uses a separate LockTimeout write-lock rather than git-remote-s3's S3 object lock.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f825864b71ca381a6","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2(e) / docs/s3-backend.md; AC line 'the auto-doctor + 60s stale-lock self-heal behavior'","norm_id":"nb9a167a999b3aeb1","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["Upstream renames the constant or ships a different default TTL, so the published '60s auto-steal' and env-var override silently mislead an operator waiting out or tuning a stale lock","git-remote-s3 >=0.3.2 uses per-reference locking with different semantics than a single global 60s TTL, making the documented self-heal narrative inaccurate"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.95,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Ground the ADR's claim that upstream `git-s3 doctor` is interactive and discards a head against the pinned git-remote-s3 version (cite the specific command/behavior) before using it to justify the custom merge-based auto-doctor.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"upstream's `git-s3 doctor` is interactive and discards a head\"","Plan: \"handled by a rebar merge-based auto-doctor because upstream's `git-s3 doctor` is interactive and discards a head\"","Retrieved upstream refs describe doctor for stale-lock cleanup (`git-remote-s3 doctor --lock-ttl`) and eliminating multiple-bundles-per-reference, but do not confirm interactive-and-discards-a-head","T1(a)/(c): a reuse-vs-build decision resting on an unverified upstream-behavior assertion"],"finding":"The ADR's central design rationale rests on the assertion that upstream's `git-s3 doctor` is 'interactive and discards a head', justifying a custom rebar merge-based auto-doctor. This is an unverified capability claim about upstream behavior that drives a build-vs-reuse decision; retrieved upstream docs describe `doctor` as a stale-lock/multiple-bundle cleanup tool but do not confirm the 'interactive' and 'discards a head' characterization. Anti-repackaging (Rule-of-Three) requires the upstream behavior be verified before rejecting reuse.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f014df2b3ed5d9809","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 (ADR rationale); AC line 3 (merge-based auto-doctor vs upstream's interactive/discarding doctor)","norm_id":"n15401e690c75e516","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer questions why rebar builds its own auto-doctor instead of invoking upstream's; the ADR cites behavior that cannot be confirmed against the pinned upstream version."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"insufficient","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_at